  speakerName: SALLY
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: '"When meeting someone new, you may also want to learn where they
    come from.

    In Ilokano, ''taga sadino ka?'' means ''where are you from?''

    Use
    it when asking someone about their hometown or place of origin.

    Listen carefully:
    taga sadino ka?

    Now, try saying ''taga sadino ka?'' yourself."

'
